  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "It's super frustrating when your kitchen cabinet installation hits a snag. Maybe the measurements seem off, or things just aren't lining up. One common issue is uneven floors or walls, which can really throw off your base cabinet and countertop heights. If you're tackling this yourself, failing to find the highest point in your floor can lead to a domino effect of problems. Another biggie is not securing wall cabinets properly into studs, which is a safety hazard for those heavy uppers, especially if you're storing lots of dishes or pantry items. Poor leveling and shimming can also cause misaligned doors and drawers, and that's a headache you definitely want to avoid. And trust me, trying to install cabinets with the doors and drawers still on makes them way heavier and harder to handle accurately. Don't forget about planning for fillers and scribe panels – a little foresight here saves a lot of headaches when it comes to appliance clearances and making everything look finished. If you're finding yourself in a pickle with any of these, don't hesitate to reach out. Sometimes, a seasoned pro like HH Remodeling LLC has the experience to spot these issues early or fix them efficiently."
    }
  ],
